WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.340
In the years since Harry Potter's story ended,
J.K.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.040
Rowling has revealed a whole lot more about
the world she created, occasionally stirring

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.800
up a little controversy along the way.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.300
Here are the biggest revelations Rowling has
shared with fans since finishing the Harry

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:14.800
Potter books.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.560
It's pretty much a hard rule that any fantasy
epic that follows the Hero's Journey has got

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:24.910
to have an old, wise man present to teach
the young protagonist how to overcome their

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:25.940
hurdles and challenges.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.180
Of course, Harry Potter is no exception.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Enter Albus Dumbledore, the headmaster of
Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.249
who begins the series watching over the orphaned
infant Harry from a distance, and eventually

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:43.500
becomes a major parental figure for the character
during their shared time at Hogwarts.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:49.480
Even after Dumbledore dies in Half Blood Prince,
his shadow looms large, all the way through

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.900
to the final moments of the series.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:55.979
Now, there's plenty Harry doesn't know about
Dumbledore, but one facet of his character

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.860
couldn't have been guessed by even the sharpest
of readers.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.040
In 2007, Rowling revealed that Dumbledore
was gay, and though fans knew he had a close

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:08.590
friendship with the wizard Grindelwald in
his younger days, most fans didn't take that

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:10.840
to mean that the two were more than friends.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.460
Though Dumbledore's orientation never needed
to be addressed by the story, this was still

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:20.280
quite a surprise for fans, who could now look
at the character in an entirely new light.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.140
Rowling even claims to have clued in one of
the films' screenwriters to this reveal, nixing

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.500
a would-be Dumbledore line about an old female
flame.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.720
After dropping the big bombshell about Dumbledore's
sexuality, Rowling waited nearly ten years

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:39.140
to push the issue again, ahead of the release
of the second film in the Potter spin-off

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.560
series, Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find
Them.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:47.300
Both Rowling and director David Yates faced
serious backlash over comments made by Yates

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:52.470
stating that Dumbledore's sexuality wouldn't
be directly addressed in the second Fantastic

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:57.580
Beasts movie, The Crimes of Grindelwald, despite
the fact that the antagonist of the film was

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.620
famously known as Dumbledore's lover.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.140
On the movie's Blu-ray release, Rowling followed
up the controversy by announcing that the

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:09.000
two had indeed engaged in an extremely intense
physical relationship.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.950
But this reveal didn't come without its controversy,
with Rowling's comments raising some important

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.840
questions about representation.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:22.000
After all, what does it say to LGBTQ fans
that Dumbledore fell in love with a murderous

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:26.000
villain and then possibly lived in celibacy
for the remainder of his life?

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.080
And why is that representation found only
on a Blu-ray special feature, rather than

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.360
within the story itself?

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.450
All in all, this particular reveal sent a
more muddled and confusing message than Rowling

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.440
likely intended.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:44.280
One of the most fascinating acts of magic
in the entire wizarding world is the Patronus

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:49.430
Charm, a difficult and advanced spell which
summons a magical protector that seems to

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.840
come from inside a wizard's own spirit.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Harry first discovers his Patronus in Prisoner
of Azkaban, where it takes the form of a stag,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:02.200
in honor of Harry's late father, James, who
could transform into that same animal.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.240
After the story officially ended, fans wanted
to know about the Patronuses of their favorite

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.610
characters, from Hermione's otter to Luna
Lovegood's rabbit, but one revelation about

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.360
a truly beloved character was particularly
tragic.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:21.380
When asked what Patronus might belong to Hogwarts
groundskeeper Rubeus Hagrid, Rowling responded

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:26.130
that Hagrid wasn't able to produce the spell
at all, likely thanks to his wrongful expulsion

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.760
from Hogwarts as a teenager.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:33.410
This wasn't Rowling's only Patronus revelation,
either, the author also noted that Severus

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:38.401
Snape was the only Death Eater who could summon
a Patronus, since he was the only member of

00:03:38.401 --> 00:03:40.640
the evil group with his soul still intact.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.180
"After all this time?"

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.340
"Always."

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:53.300
Harry Potter fans still have plenty of lingering
questions about the wizarding world, and,

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.500
to her credit, Rowling has answered many of
them.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.820
But she has also answered a few questions
nobody ever asked.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:04.040
Despite bathrooms playing a weirdly significant
role in the series, fans weren't exactly clamouring

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.020
to find out how wizards got along before the
days of indoor plumbing.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.280
Even so, Rowling was on hand to clear that
one up…so to speak.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:17.220
In early 2019, a tweet from Harry Potter website
Pottermore revealed a pretty unexpected fact

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.400
about the wizarding world.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.940
Apparently, before wizards began using Muggle-style
plumbing, they basically just went right on

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:27.140
the floor, and then got rid of it using a
vanishing spell.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:31.240
Weirdly enough, this wasn't actually new information,
either.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.460
Pottermore had previously revealed this in
a 2015 essay on the website, but the 2019

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:41.260
tweet caused far more of a stir, with many
fans wondering why it even needed to be said.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.340
Every long-running series needs an iconic
villain, and Voldemort's certainly fit the

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.560
bill for Harry Potter.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.500
After trying to kill Harry as an infant and
nearly perishing himself, Voldemort spends

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.840
the rest of his life on a mission to defeat
Harry once and for all.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:05:00.160
When Harry hears a prophecy about the two
in Order of the Phoenix, he realizes that

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.300
he can't avoid his fate.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.840
"For neither can live while the other survives."

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:11.760
After destroying Voldemort's Horcruxes and
sacrificing himself to defeat the evil wizard,

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:17.000
Harry is finally able to best Voldemort once
and for all, taking down one of the most nefarious

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.960
and murderous wizards the world had ever seen.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:25.240
In fact, Voldemort was so nefarious and murderous
that most wizards refused to even speak his

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:30.460
name, instead, many of them simply referred
to him as "He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named" or "You-Know-Who."

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:31.860
"Voldemort."

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.540
"Voldemort?"

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.540
"Shh."

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:40.480
As it turns out, however, even those bold
enough to say "Voldemort" have been getting

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.340
it all wrong.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:46.880
In 2015, Rowling revealed she always meant
Voldemort to be pronounced in the French fashion

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:52.210
with a silent T, vohl-duh-MORE, since the
name itself means "flight of death", referring

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.840
to the dark wizard's own fear of death.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.500
Pretty much everyone has actually been pronouncing
it incorrectly, from the fans to the films

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.000
themselves.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:05.440
Hermione Granger has served as an inspiration
to brilliant and bookish children ever since

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.500
her introduction in the first book in the
series.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:12.400
Though she initially comes off as a frustrating
know-it-all to Harry and Ron, Hermione quickly

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.980
becomes one of the series' most virtuous and
likeable characters.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:17.620
"Mental, that one.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.380
I'm telling you."

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:24.590
Heralded as the brightest witch of her age,
Hermione's love of learning and quick thinking

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:29.759
set her apart from other students, even earning
her a valuable and powerful Time-Turner in

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.440
her third year at Hogwarts.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:36.480
Hermione's ingenuity serves the trio particularly
well in Deathly Hallows, when she secretly

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:41.740
packs all of their most valuable belongings
into a tiny beaded evening bag, which she

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.280
has bewitched to hold an enormous amount of
objects.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:49.560
Though this magical object proves crucial
in the final push to defeat Voldemort, it

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:54.850
turns out that Hermione actually broke wizarding
law by putting an extension charm on the bag,

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.940
although she was never taken to task for it.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.080
Probably because people had bigger things
on their mind.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:05.180
Even after the Harry Potter series ended,
the concept of sorting has played a big role

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:09.560
in a post-Potter world, with pretty much every
Potter fan out there sorting themselves into

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.620
one of Hogwarts' four personality-based houses.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:18.260
Whether you're a brave Gryffindor, a hardworking
Hufflepuff, a brilliant Ravenclaw, or a cunning

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:22.220
Slytherin, most fans know which house they
identify with the most.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:27.600
And when Pottermore debuted in 2011, it featured
the first ever definitive sorting quiz, written

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.640
by Rowling herself.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:31.260
For most people, sorting is fairly straightforward.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:36.220
Still, Rowling used Pottermore to reveal the
concept of a "Hatstall," which happens when

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:41.660
a person who shares traits that fit into multiple
houses causes the Sorting Hat to get stuck

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:45.800
on where to place them, sometimes for more
than five minutes.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:49.220
Even though the hat struggled with Harry,
Harry isn't considered a Hatstall.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:54.639
Hermione nearly was, as the hat struggled
to choose between Gryffindor and Ravenclaw.

00:07:54.639 --> 00:07:59.840
His classmate Neville Longbottom's long sorting
process, meanwhile, came down to a fight between

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.440
Neville and the hat over whether or not he
was brave enough for Gryffindor.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:05.180
Spoiler alert: he was.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:10.210
As it turned out, however, Harry actually
did know two Hatstalls, his Transfiguration

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:15.100
professor Minerva McGonagall and his parents'
own personal Judas, Peter Pettigrew.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.520
Both ended up in Gryffindor, after nearly
ending up in Ravenclaw and Slytherin, respectively.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:26.280
Fans have asked plenty of questions about
Hogwarts itself over the years, but one particular

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.660
issue seems to have weighed heavy on their
minds.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.220
What do students actually do before they enroll
at the school?

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:36.320
Since students don't start at Hogwarts until
they hit 11 years of age, many fans wondered

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:41.040
what young magical children did before their
seven-year schooling career began.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:45.380
In an interview with Time after the book series
came to a close, Rowling answered several

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:49.820
remaining questions about the books, and one
revelation cleared up this exact question.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:54.400
During the interview, Rowling confirmed that
young wizarding children are homeschooled,

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:58.480
since many younger witches and wizards have
trouble controlling their magic, and must

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.640
be kept at home so they don't reveal themselves
to Muggles by mistake.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.680
Before Harry learns that he's a wizard and
starts attending Hogwarts, he spends 11 miserable

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:12.840
years living with his Aunt Petunia and Uncle
Vernon, as well as their son Dudley.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:18.370
The Dursleys all despise Harry and treat him
terribly, even forcing the orphan to sleep

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:21.000
in a spider-ridden cupboard under the stairs.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.300
It is later revealed that Petunia was jealous
of her sister's magical ability, despite frequently

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.640
calling Lily a "freak."

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:33.140
Her detestable husband Vernon is equally incensed
by the magical world, with the two of them

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:38.220
swearing that they'll never let Harry be a
wizard...until Hogwarts eventually intervenes.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.420
"You're a wizard, Harry."

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:45.410
Even with the specter of magic hanging over
them, it's still a bit baffling that Vernon

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:49.680
and Petunia would be so angry and resentful
to a small child.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:54.200
Rowling eventually revealed that issues between
the Dursleys and Harry's parents went all

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:59.290
the way back to a double date gone wrong,
during which James antagonized the Dursleys

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.700
to the point of no return.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:06.000
As he grows up, Harry's growing resemblance
to his father infuriates the Dursleys, and

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.590
Uncle Vernon in particular.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:13.839
One of the strangest figures that lives within
Hogwarts' walls has got to be Moaning Myrtle,

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.740
the ghost of a young girl killed by the basilisk
that resides inside the Chamber of Secrets.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:23.260
Clearly, Myrtle has had some trouble letting
go, since she haunts the very bathroom where

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:27.769
she died, and she spends her time wreaking
havoc, haunting students and generally being

00:10:27.769 --> 00:10:28.620
kinda annoying.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:33.240
Thanks to this, Myrtle is generally considered
one of the school's least-liked ghosts.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:37.840
At one point, Rowling decided to reveal Myrtle's
full name, which was previously unknown to

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:38.340
readers.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:43.440
Taking to Twitter, the author announced that
Myrtle's name is actually Myrtle Elizabeth

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:48.470
Warren, though she was quick to disavow any
relation between Hogwarts' weirdest ghost

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:50.220
and the accomplished American senator.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:55.510
While the books were still being written,
diehard fans engaged in constant arguments

00:10:55.510 --> 00:11:00.279
about Hermione's love life, hotly debating
whether she should end up with Harry or Ron.

00:11:00.279 --> 00:11:04.130
By the time the later books in the series
came around, however, it had become relatively

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:06.279
clear in which direction Rowling was leaning.

00:11:06.279 --> 00:11:09.790
"Hermione's got nice skin, wouldn't you say,
as skin goes, I mean."

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.450
"I've never really thought about it, but I
suppose, yeah.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:14.780
I think I'll be going to sleep now."

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:15.520
"Right, yeah."

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:20.400
In the end, she paired Hermione with Ron,
capitalizing on their years of tension and

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.400
many differences.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:25.800
Harry, meanwhile, ended up with Ginny, Ron's
feisty and talented younger sister.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:30.000
However, Rowling has since changed course,
saying she wished Hermione had ended up with

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.640
Harry after all.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:35.170
She claimed that the relationship between
Ron and Hermione was simply a form of "wish

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:38.740
fulfillment" for her, vindicating some fans
while infuriating others.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:43.740
For fans who loved the fiery, intense relationship
between Ron and Hermione, however, this felt

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.400
like a total betrayal by Rowling.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:49.840
To date, this incident is counted as one of
the most famous examples of Rowling making

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:54.000
an unnecessary reveal, one that many fans
wished she had kept to herself.

